<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rigoberta Menchú</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1959</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rigoberta Menchú (born 1959) is a K'iche' Maya activist from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> who received the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 1992 for her work for indigenous rights and reconciliation. Several members of her family, including her father, who died in the burning of the Spanish embassy in 1980, were killed by the security forces during the civil war. Her testimony I, Rigoberta Menchú made the war known abroad.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rigoberta-menchu.jpg" alt="Rigoberta Menchú" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gobierno de Guatemala · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20240620_NP_PRESIDENTE_BERNARDO_AREVALO_Y_KARIN_HERRERA_PARTICIPAN_EN_DIALOGO_PREMIO_NOBEL_DE_LA_PAZ_054_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
